 140:Core/Src/dsp_task.c **** 
 141:Core/Src/dsp_task.c **** /* Granular overlap-add (OLA) pitch shifter.
 142:Core/Src/dsp_task.c ****    Two read heads advance through a circular delay buffer at 'ratio' samples/step
 143:Core/Src/dsp_task.c ****    (ratio = 2^(semitones/12)).  When the primary head drifts too close to the write
 144:Core/Src/dsp_task.c ****    pointer (pitch up) or too far behind it (pitch down), a secondary head is placed
 145:Core/Src/dsp_task.c ****    PITCH_GRAIN samples away and crossfaded in over PITCH_OVERLAP samples, then the
 146:Core/Src/dsp_task.c ****    primary head snaps to the secondary position.  Linear interpolation gives sub-sample
 147:Core/Src/dsp_task.c ****    accuracy.  24-bit layout: L_MSW at i, L_LSW at i+1, R_MSW at i+2, R_LSW at i+3. */
